 "title": "DUCK",
 "category": "Sound",
 "author": "hugz202 (AE-analog-rytm-mods); MKII port: Iced-Cream",
 "license": "MIT",
 "description": "Sidechain-style pumping without the analog compressor: every audio block the other voices' analog VCA words are scaled by a gain that dips when the key track's voice hits. FX track, AMP (COMP) pressed twice: the DUCK page, SRC (OFF or the key track), DEP, ATK, HLD, REL. From 1.1 (core-ar2 0.10) the five are saved with the kit (SRC OFF in a new kit) and are the FX track's lockable parameters: p-locked with an FX trig held, locked in scenes and performances, on MIDI as NRPNs; DEP, ATK, HLD and REL are FX LFO destinations, SRC jumps and is not. The key is the source voice's own audio as the codec captured it, one block late; the delay and reverb returns are not ducked. Its knobs are the hidden HH TEST machine's parameter records, renamed. Needs core-ar2 0.10 (its page tables, lockable parameters and 39 of the kit's 64 bits), so it cannot share a build with fx-sends 1.1. Shares the COMP page list with comp-preview 1.1. Port of AE-analog-rytm-mods 0012-duck (Analog Rytm MK1).",
 "device": "analog-rytm-mk2",
 "os": "1.74",
